{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "conservative_overlap_gated_clusters_4_to_2",
    "description": "Conformance fixture: the CANDIDATE-GATED pathway of regridding/conservative_overlap.esm with GENUINE broad-phase pruning. Geometry: two disjoint cell clusters ten degrees apart -- cluster A: source cells [0,1]x[0,1] and [1,2]x[0,1] coarsened into target [0,2]x[0,1]; cluster B: source cells [10,11]x[0,1] and [11,12]x[0,1] coarsened into target [10,12]x[0,1] (planar manifold, all cells unit-height 2:1 coarsenings). BROAD PHASE with bin_dx = bin_dy = 4.0 and bbox-min-corner representatives (derived in-library by the reduce-min templates): cluster-A representatives (lon 0, 1) quantize to floor bin 0, cluster-B representatives (lon 10, 11) to floor bin 2 -- so the bin-Skolem equi-join admits only the four same-cluster pairs and PRUNES the four cross-cluster pairs, which the gated narrow phase NEVER CLIPS (this is the O(#candidates) saving made observable: 4 clips instead of 8). The binning is ADMISSIBLE because the pruned pairs have zero true overlap (the clusters are disjoint), so the dense path -- computed side by side on the same rings -- reaches the identical surviving set: it clips all 8 pairs, gets exactly 0 for the cross-cluster four, and the sliver filter drops them. The inline test gated_equals_dense asserts the total L1 residual across A_ij/A_j/W_ij is 0.0 EXACTLY (tolerance abs 0.0), which is the esm-spec 8.6.1 dense/gated value-identity under an admissible binning, on geometry where the candidate set is a PROPER SUBSET of the cross product (unlike the degenerate-safe sibling conservative_overlap_gated_3x3_to_2x2 where the candidate set is full). Hand geometry: each target is tiled by exactly its two cluster's source cells, A_ij = 1.0 deg^2 for the four surviving pairs, A_j = 2.0, W_ij = 1/2, F_tgt = [(1+2)/2, (3+4)/2] = [1.5, 3.5] with F_src = [1..4], both masses 10 (unit source areas). Partition-of-unity and conservation are the 5.8.3 EXACT gates (the targets tile the source domain); the golden per-pair weights come from the official Julia runner via scripts/regenerate-goldens.sh.",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "regridding",
      "conservative_overlap",
      "broad-phase",
      "bin-skolem",
      "candidate-gated",
      "candidate-pruning",
      "join",
      "value-identity",
      "template-import",
      "partition-of-unity",
      "conservation"
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Regrid": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../../../../regridding/conservative_overlap.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NSRC": 4,
            "NTGT": 2,
            "NVERT": 4
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "atol": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1e-12,
          "description": "Sliver floor (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.8.2): 1e-12 deg^2 against true overlaps of 1.0 deg^2. Shared by the gated and dense assembly templates so the surviving sets coincide."
        },
        "bin_dx": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 4.0,
          "description": "Broad-phase bin width (degrees lon): 4.0 separates the clusters (representatives 0,1 -> bin 0; 10,11 -> bin 2) while keeping each cluster's source and target representatives in a common bin -- an ADMISSIBLE, genuinely PRUNING binning."
        },
        "bin_dy": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 4.0,
          "description": "Broad-phase bin height (degrees lat): all representatives at lat 0 -> bin 0."
        },
        "src_poly": {
          "type": "observed",
          "shape": [
            "src_cells",
            "overlap_cell_verts",
            "overlap_coord"
          ],
          "description": "Source-cell geometry: four closed CCW lon-lat rings in two disjoint clusters -- [0,1] and [1,2] (cluster A), [10,11] and [11,12] (cluster B), all x [0,1] in lat.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "const",
            "value": [
